gpui: Let the running app apply theme overrides live over host.call

Against longbridge/nsh e626a8d (0.4.0), after patches 0001-0003. The
embedding API (`AppView::set_theme` / `set_theme_json`) already replaces
a surface's live theme tokens at once, in both appearances, with the
app's own classes resolving again and no rebuild (docs/dev/embedding.md
"The host's theme in NSH"). The development host (`nsh-gpui-host`, this
patch's `open_app_window`) wired no handler onto `AppOptions::host` at
all, so the running app had no way to reach it: `host.call` of any name
rejected at once (`nsh_engine::host_channel::EngineBridge::call`), and
`host.available()` stayed false.

This registers one handler, `theme.setOverrides(json | null)`, on every
window `open_app_window` opens (the generic development host, unlike an
embedding host's own `AppView::host()` calls, which still add their own
handlers to the same channel undisturbed). `null` clears back to the
app's theme; otherwise `json` is the theme file shadcn's `cssVars` is
(`nsh.json`'s `"theme"` shape): parsed with `nsh_base::Theme::from_json`,
which already keeps every token the file carries (the app's flattened
alpha and radius tokens included, not a fixed shadcn subset) in its
`Tokens` map, so nothing the live apply needs is lost against the
embedding path. Registering the handler marks the channel `available()`
(`HostChannel::handle`), which is the capability an app's TS checks
before trying a live apply instead of its rebuild-and-restart fallback;
a host without this patch never registers it, so `available()` stays
false there and the app's existing fallback is unchanged.

The handler runs on the engine thread (`HostChannel::handle`'s own
contract), which cannot touch the surface (`Rc`, `RefCell`: main-thread
only, per `AppView`'s doc "call them through view.update(cx, ...)").
JSON validity is checked right there (`Theme::from_json` touches no GPUI
state), so a malformed theme rejects the call instead of silently doing
nothing; a valid one is handed to the existing main-thread job queue
(`crate::rt::invoke`, already used for cross-thread work such as decoded
images) and, once there, to `crate::rt::on_app` for the `&mut App`
`set_theme_json` / `set_theme` need. Both hops are the crate's own
established pattern (`rt.rs`); no new dependency, no change to
`Cargo.lock` (satisfies `cargo build --locked`).

Verified in a real window (third_party/nsh-host/README.md "live theme";
screenshots under workspace/live-theme/): every built-in theme (T3 Code,
T3 Chat, Grove, Ocean, Ember, Iris) in both light and dark, contrast,
and a menu, all recolour without the window restarting (same pid
throughout); the stock host (no T3GPUI_HOST) still rebuilds and
restarts, unchanged.

## Public API

- `theme.setOverrides(json: object | null)`: a new `host.call` name the
  development host's `AppOptions::host` channel answers (any app that
  declares it in `nsh.json`'s `capabilities.host`). Applies a theme file
  (shadcn's `cssVars`) to the running window's live tokens at once, or
  clears back to the app's own theme (`null`); rejects (`ERR_NSH_HOST_ERROR`)
  for a theme file that does not parse.

--- a/crates/gpui/nsh-platform-gpui/src/app.rs	2026-11-12 14:20:10
+++ b/crates/gpui/nsh-platform-gpui/src/app.rs	2026-11-12 14:20:10
@@ -908,9 +908,71 @@
         },
         ..Default::default()
     };
+    // `theme.setOverrides(json | null)`: the running app's `host.call` of
+    // this name replaces this view's live theme tokens, in every
+    // appearance, at once (`AppView::set_theme_json` below already applies
+    // without a rebuild; what was missing was a way for `host.call` to
+    // reach it in the development host, which wires no handlers of its
+    // own). Registering it here, unconditionally, marks `options.host`
+    // `available()` (`nsh_engine::HostChannel::handle`), which is the
+    // capability signal an app's TS checks before trying a live apply
+    // instead of its rebuild-and-restart fallback; an embedding app that
+    // also calls `AppOptions::host`'s `handle` for its own names (as
+    // `dialogs.pickFolder`, say) keeps those, `handle` only replaces the
+    // handler of the name it is given.
+    let theme_host = options.host.clone();
     let handle = cx.open_window(window_options, move |window, cx| {
         let view: Entity<AppView> = cx.new(|cx| AppView::new(options, window, cx));
         view.read(cx).own_window(window, cx);
+        {
+            let weak = view.downgrade();
+            theme_host.handle("theme.setOverrides", move |call| {
+                // `null` clears back to the app's own theme; anything else
+                // must be a theme file `nsh_base::Theme::from_json` reads
+                // (shadcn's `cssVars`: `theme`, `light`, `dark`, every name
+                // it carries, the app's flattened alpha and radius tokens
+                // included, since `Theme` keeps the whole parsed `Tokens`
+                // map, not a fixed shadcn subset). Checked eagerly (on this,
+                // the engine thread: `Theme::from_json` touches no GPUI
+                // state) so a malformed theme rejects the call instead of
+                // silently doing nothing.
+                let json: Option<String> = match call.data() {
+                    serde_json::Value::Null => None,
+                    other => Some(other.to_string()),
+                };
+                if let Some(json) = &json
+                    && let Err(err) = nsh_base::Theme::from_json(json)
+                {
+                    call.reject(err.to_string());
+                    return;
+                }
+                call.resolve(serde_json::Value::Null);
+                // The engine thread cannot touch the surface (`Rc`,
+                // `RefCell`, main-thread only): hand the already-validated
+                // json to the main thread's job queue (`crate::rt::invoke`,
+                // any thread), then, now on the main thread, to its async
+                // app handle (`crate::rt::on_app`) for the `&mut App`
+                // `set_theme_json` / `set_theme` need.
+                let weak = weak.clone();
+                crate::rt::invoke(move || {
+                    let weak = weak.clone();
+                    let json = json.clone();
+                    crate::rt::on_app(move |cx| {
+                        let Some(view) = weak.upgrade() else {
+                            return;
+                        };
+                        view.update(cx, |view, cx| match &json {
+                            Some(json) => {
+                                if let Err(err) = view.set_theme_json(json, cx) {
+                                    log::warn!("theme.setOverrides: {err}");
+                                }
+                            }
+                            None => view.set_theme(None, cx),
+                        });
+                    });
+                });
+            });
+        }
         match source {
             AppSource::Rust(root) => view.read(cx).load(App::Rust(root)),
             AppSource::Bundle(bundle) => view.read(cx).load(App::Js(bundle)),
